{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Ada Script"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Testing Ada Script"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/adascripting\/adascripttesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write tests next to your gameplay code, run them with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift test"},{"type":"text","text":" or a command, and keep them out of shipped builds."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"ECS Integration","anchor":"ECS-Integration","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptECS","doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptDiagnosticsAndPerformance"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A function annotated with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a test. It takes no parameters and may sit in any ","type":"text"},{"code":".ada","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file, where it can see that file’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"private","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declarations, or under a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tests\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directory, where it sees public declarations only.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@system(id: \"gravity\")","class GravitySystem {","    @query(Body)","    var bodies;","","    func update(context) { \/* … *\/ }","}","","private func clampSpeed(speed) { return Math.max(speed, -50.0); }","","@test(\"speed is capped\")","func speedIsCapped() {","    expectEqual(clampSpeed(-100.0), -50.0);","}"],"syntax":"ada"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Assertions","level":3,"text":"Assertions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"expect(condition)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectEqual(actual, expected)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectNear(actual, expected, tolerance)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectNil(value)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"fail(message)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" record a failure and let the test continue. ","type":"text"},{"code":"require(condition)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" records a failure and ends the test. Each failure is reported as ","type":"text"},{"code":"path:line:column: message","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"TestWorld","level":3,"text":"TestWorld"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"TestWorld()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" creates an isolated world with the module’s components and systems. Time moves only when the test says so.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Run synchronous ","type":"text"},{"code":"TestWorld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" steps on the host. Browser players cannot block their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single thread while awaiting the scheduler; they report a diagnostic if asked to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"step a test world. Gameplay systems continue through the normal async frame loop.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@test(\"a body falls\")","func falls() {","    var world = TestWorld();","    var body = world.spawn([Body(y: 10.0, speed: 0.0)]);","    world.run(30);","    expect(world.read(body, \"Body\", \"y\") < 10.0);","}"],"syntax":"ada"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"spawn(components)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert(entity, component)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"remove(entity, name)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"despawn(entity)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" change entities at once.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"has(entity, name)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"read(entity, name, field)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"count(name)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inspect them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"run(ticks)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" installs every system and runs fixed 1\/60 s ticks. ","type":"text"},{"code":"runSystem(System, ticks)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" installs only that system. ","type":"text"},{"code":"advance(seconds)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs one step of an exact length.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each test gets its own world. Module-level ","type":"text"},{"code":"var","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values that are numbers, booleans, strings or null are restored after each test; lists and maps are not.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Tests-directory","level":3,"text":"The Tests directory"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Files under ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tests\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are compiled only when tests run, and gameplay code cannot import from them.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Running-tests","level":3,"text":"Running tests"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Load a project with tests and run it from Swift:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let plugin = try AdaScriptPlugin(sources: sources, name: \"Game\", includeTests: true)","let results = plugin.runTests()"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"or point ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestProject","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" at a directory, which picks up every ","type":"text"},{"code":".ada","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" file, and render the outcome with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestReport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" as text, JUnit or JSON. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdaScriptTest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" command does the same from a terminal and exits non-zero on failure:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["swift run AdaScriptTest Path\/To\/Project --format junit"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Production modules never contain tests. Loading without ","type":"text"},{"code":"includeTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes every ","type":"text"},{"code":"@test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tests\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directory, and reports any gameplay code that refers to a test-only name such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"expect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"TestWorld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Running tests","anchor":"Running-tests","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestProject","doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestReport","doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestCase","doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestResult"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://AdaScripting/documentation/AdaScripting/AdaScriptTestReport":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Text, JUnit and JSON renderings of test results, for terminals and CI."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdaScriptTestReport"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestReport","url":"\/documentation\/adascripting\/adascripttestreport","title":"AdaScriptTestReport","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdaScriptTestReport"}]},"doc://AdaScripting/documentation/AdaScripting/AdaScriptTestResult":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The outcome of running one ","type":"text"},{"code":"@test","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdaScriptTestResult","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestResult","url":"\/documentation\/adascripting\/adascripttestresult","title":"AdaScriptTestResult","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AdaScriptTestResult","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://AdaScripting/documentation/AdaScripting/AdaScriptTestCase":{"url":"\/documentation\/adascripting\/adascripttestcase","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestCase","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdaScriptTestCase","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AdaScriptTestCase","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"One ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@test"},{"type":"text","text":" function discovered in an Ada Script module (ADR-0024)."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdaScriptTestCase"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AdaScripting/documentation/AdaScripting/AdaScriptECS":{"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare annotation-driven systems and iterate native AdaECS component columns."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptECS","url":"\/documentation\/adascripting\/adascriptecs","title":"Ada Script ECS"},"doc://AdaScripting/documentation/AdaScripting/AdaScriptTestProject":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@test"},{"type":"text","text":" functions of an Ada Script project on disk (ADR-0024)."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdaScriptTestProject"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptTestProject","url":"\/documentation\/adascripting\/adascripttestproject","title":"AdaScriptTestProject","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdaScriptTestProject"}]},"doc://AdaScripting/documentation/AdaScripting":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting","url":"\/documentation\/adascripting","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write gameplay systems in Ada Script while keeping entity filtering and access planning in AdaEngine’s native ECS."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Ada Script"},"doc://AdaScripting/documentation/AdaScripting/AdaScriptDiagnosticsAndPerformance":{"abstract":[{"text":"Understand annotation, setup, and runtime failures and keep ECS work on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"native chunk path.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adascripting\/adascriptdiagnosticsandperformance","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaScripting\/documentation\/AdaScripting\/AdaScriptDiagnosticsAndPerformance","title":"Ada Script Diagnostics and Performance","role":"article"}}}